  "body": "## What changed\n\n**Stacked on #595** (issue #585, the `Columns` seam). Merge #595 first. This is M7.3 step 3/6 (#26), **in part**.\n\nThe app's stock **readers** now read through the `Columns` seam instead of indexing a `Dexel` directly:\n\n| Reader | Where |\n|---|---|\n| `prior_top` | `operation/top_stock.rs`: the prior top over a region |\n| `revolved_surface` | `operation/drill_prior.rs`: a lathe axial hole's revolved prior |\n| `columns_reach` | `operation/carried_stock.rs`: carried columns over a footprint |\n| `carried_body_bounds` | `rest/across.rs`: the carried body's bounds |\n\nThey use the same lattice formulas (`Columns::cell`/`origin`/`center`/`col`/`top_at`), so **the answers are unchanged**. Callers wrap their grid with `Columns::of_grid`.\n\n**Not in this PR: the holders.** Every app stock holder is either a plain grid or the **carried `Body`** (sim `carry.rs`). That's a two-sided column store with lattice flips and mirrors, which the app mutates directly (`simulate(&mut body.dex, ..)`, `lower`). Moving it onto `Stock` is a data-model design, not a seam move, so it's filed as **#637** with its open questions. #586 closes when #637 lands, so this PR is `Refs`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **`scripts/gate.sh quick`:** the sim and app suites pass, **1850 passed, 0 failed**.\n- **Named:**\n\n  | Suite | Passed |\n  |---|---|\n  | drill_prior | 12 |\n  | drill_reach | 6 |\n  | carried_verify | 8 |\n  | setup_carry | 9 |\n  | top_stock | 4 |\n  | rest_across_setups | 7 |\n  | suppressed_rest | 2 |\n  | stock_sim_document | 9 |\n  | `--lib top_stock` | 5 |\n  | sim prior_columns | 2 |\n\n- **Clippy** on app and sim with `-D warnings`: clean. No golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNothing user-visible: it's a behaviour-neutral refactor.\n\nChangelog: none (internal refactor, behaviour-neutral)\n\nRefs #586\nRefs #26\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
